  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s21/bf96dc86> ;
  triage:notes "Origin sprint feature/pAG-s20-move-deferred-policy-out-of-transport @ 50572166: crates/atm-daemon/src/peer_transport/tests/transport_client.rs asserts resume_pending_replay(), persist_replay_request(), and AtmErrorCode::RemoteDeliveryOutcomeUnknown directly at the transport-test layer -- 18 matches. Downstream presence checked across the ordered ladder: s21 (feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing @ bf96dc86, dev in progress, merge-forward of s20 only, no new dev commits yet) carries 15 matches -- defect inherited unchanged, not yet remediated. s22-s25 (feature/pAG-s22-host-resolution-boundary, feature/pAG-s23-remove-synthetic-deferred-receipts, feature/pAG-s24-preserve-request-shape, feature/pAG-s25-live-two-daemon-proof) are all still pinned at baseline 03c873fc (not started, have not branched forward past AG.18-AG.21), so the defect is present there only via the same shared baseline file, not yet as an inherited-and-untouched sprint occurrence -- re-check when those sprints branch forward. Per team fix-dispatch policy (fix dispatch targets latest sprint branch, never integrate; merge-forward closes lower occurrences), promote_to_branch is set to the highest currently-open branch with real commits, feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing @ bf96dc86 -- same branch as AG20-BLOCK-001/002/003. dispatchReady is false: per pattern note this finding is blocked on AG20-BLOCK-001/002/003 landing the real policy/persistence relocation first; the test-surface rewrite is meaningless (and risks masking the underlying defect) until the production code it should assert against has actually moved out of the transport layer. Dispatch AG20-BLOCK-004 as one fix unit together with AG20-BLOCK-001/002/003, not standalone, then merge-forward to close all occurrences. Re-verify by re-grepping transport_client.rs for resume_pending_replay/persist_replay_request/RemoteDeliveryOutcomeUnknown after the fix lands -- do not mark closed on the presence of any rewritten test file alone; confirm the assertions target the new policy-owning surface, not the transport layer." .

